    "probe_text": "## `POST /api/owners` \u2014 ordered validations and side-effects\n\nThe whole pipeline (`owners.POST.yml`) runs under one transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]` on every step), so all writes commit once at the end.\n\n**0. Authorization (endpoint guard)**\n- Requires `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`; otherwise the request is rejected before any step runs.\n\n**1. `ValidateOwnerFields`** \u2014 reads the request body (the one and only `@RequestBody` bind), then:\n- *Validation:* `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must each be non-null and non-blank \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400, naming every missing field).\n- *Side-effect + validation:* normalizes `telephone` to E.164 via `OwnerTelephone.toE164` and **writes it back onto the body**. Rules: strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps an explicit `+<country>`; otherwise assumes `+61` and drops one leading `0`; result must be 8\u201315 digits \u2192 else `InvalidOwnerTelephoneException` (400).\n- *Side-effect + validation:* if `email` is present (non-blank) it must match the email pattern and is **stored lower-cased** \u2192 else `InvalidOwnerEmailException` (400); an absent email is allowed.\n- *Side-effect:* republishes the mutated body as a variable for later steps.\n\n**2. `EnsureUniqueOwnerTelephone`**\n- *Validation:* loads all owners and rejects if the canonical E.164 telephone already belongs to any existing owner \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException` (409).\n\n**3. `EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold`**\n- *Validation:* unless the request set `sharesHousehold` true (which bypasses the check), rejects if `lastName` + `address` match an existing owner, compared case-insensitively with collapsed/trimmed whitespace \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException` (409).\n\n**4. `BuildOwner`**\n- *Side-effect:* maps the DTO to a new `Owner` entity; if `registrationDate` is null, sets it to `LocalDate.now()`.\n\n**5. `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`**\n- *Side-effect:* sets `customerCode` = `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where `LAST3` is the upper-cased first three letters of the last name and `NNNN` is zero-padded `(current owner count + 1)`. Runs before save so the new owner isn't yet counted. Mutates the entity in place.\n\n**6. `SaveOwner`**\n- *Side-effect:* persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save`.\n\n**7. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`**\n- *Side-effect:* maps the saved owner to `OwnerDto` and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nAny of the four checked exceptions above are turned into their HTTP responses by the matching handlers in `officefloor/escalation/`."
